---
import SiteLayout from '../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
import Figure from '../components/Figure.astro';
import Calc from '../components/Calc.astro';
const faq = [
 {
  "q": "Has the 8th Pay Commission been implemented?",
  "a": "No. The commission was constituted on 3 November 2025 and is still working on its report, which is due within 18 months. Revised pay cannot start until the government accepts the recommendations and notifies new rules."
 },
 {
  "q": "What is the current DA for central government employees?",
  "a": "63% of basic pay from 1 July 2026. It was 60% from 1 January 2026 and 58% before that."
 },
 {
  "q": "What is the fitment factor for the 8th Pay Commission?",
  "a": "There is no official figure yet. Estimates in the media range from about 1.8 to 2.86 or higher, but they are projections and not government decisions."
 },
 {
  "q": "Are the calculators on this site official?",
  "a": "No. They are independent tools that estimate pay using 7th CPC rules and assumed 8th CPC scenarios. Official pay will follow the notified pay matrix and rules."
 }
];
const toc = [];
const related = [];
---

<SiteLayout title="8th Pay Commission 2026: Salary Calculator, DA, Fitment, Pay Matrix" description="Independent 8th Pay Commission guides: salary, arrears and pension calculators, DA at 63%, fitment factor scenarios, pay matrix and verified updates." slug="" h1="8th Pay Commission 2026" lead="Calculators, DA rate and plain-English updates." faq={faq} toc={toc} related={related} pageType="home" alternate="hi/8th-pay-commission">

<section class="hero">
<h1>8th Pay Commission 2026: Calculators, DA Rate and Plain-English Updates</h1>
<p>Independent guides for central government employees and pensioners. We separate what is officially confirmed from what is only a projection, so you can plan without guessing.</p>
<div class="btns"><a class="btn" href="/8th-pay-commission-salary-calculator/">Salary calculator</a><a class="btn alt" href="/8th-pay-commission-latest-news/">Latest news</a><a class="btn alt" href="/da-hike-latest-news/">DA hike: 63%</a><a class="btn alt" href="/hi/8th-pay-commission/">हिंदी में पढ़ें</a></div>
</section>

<div class="answer"><p><strong>Where things stand (3 November 2026):</strong> The 8th Central Pay Commission was constituted on 3 November 2025 under Justice Ranjana Prakash Desai and has 18 months to report, which points to around May 2027. No fitment factor, new pay matrix or payout date has been announced. Dearness Allowance stands at 63% from 1 July 2026.</p></div>

