<h2 id="known-unknown">What is confirmed and what is not</h2>
<div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Question</th><th>Status</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row">Has the commission been formed?</th><td>Confirmed</td><td>Terms of Reference notified on 3 November 2025; chair, one part-time member and a member-secretary named.</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">When is the report due?</th><td>Confirmed window</td><td>Within 18 months of constitution, so about May 2027. Interim reports are allowed.</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">What is the fitment factor?</th><td>Not announced</td><td>Figures such as 1.92, 2.28 or 2.86 are projections by analysts and staff bodies, not government numbers.</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">From when will revised pay apply?</th><td>Not confirmed</td><td>Media reports say 1 January 2026 is the expected reference date. The government has not notified it.</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">What is DA today?</th><td>Confirmed</td><td>63% from 1 July 2026, approved by the Union Cabinet on 28 October 2026.</td></tr></tbody></table></div>

